me at `-O2`) rather than \"fixing\" it — confirmed by byte-exact transcripts. `FINDINGS.md` records this and four other investigated non-divergences so the distinction is auditable.\n- My first stdout comparison failed spuriously: libtest's own progress output from a parallel thread leaked into the fd-1 capture window. That was my harness's flaw, not the translation's. Fixed with `RUST_TEST_THREADS=1` in `.cargo/config.toml` plus a contamination detector that reports the cause instead of a phantom divergence.\n\nThere are no `[features]` and no `#ifdef`s anywhere, so the feature axis collapses to one configuration; `verify.sh` enumerates the powerset generically and covers both profiles. `c_src/` is byte-for-byte unmodified (md5 verified).","ttft_ms":2725,"ttft_stream_ms":2533,"time_to_request_ms":38,"type":"result","duration_ms":1613551,"uuid":"4d6e7f0b-c069-430d-bf39-09dc662f71fb","queued_turn_count":0}
